MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Decoded from wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485:

- The loader (GH 0x1402873f0) takes every MDLV version up to 0023. A mesh's vertex layout comes
  from its format word (the component tables at 0x1404c4da0 / 0x1404c4e10: position, normal,
  tangent, blend indices, weights, texcoords, colour), read from the header before MDLV0015, after
  it from 0015, after the bounds from 0017; flag bit 0 = 32-bit indices. LWE took only
  MDLV0021/0023, found the vertex block by a byte scan and assumed 80-byte vertices and 16-bit
  indices, so 7 of the 14 puppet scenes drew their raw sprite sheet (G07).
- Sections follow the meshes, each a tag and the offset of its end. MDLS: bones (name, flags,
  parent, the bind matrix relative to the parent, a JSON string), then IK targets and constraints
  from version 2. MDLA: per animation an id, name, mode (loop / mirror / single), fps, frame count,
  flags and one track per bone of frames + 1 samples (position, Euler angles WE turns into a
  quaternion R = Rz·Ry·Rx, scale), then per version the target, constraint, curve, bone-alpha,
  blend-shape and range blocks and the events. MDAT: attachments (bone, name, matrix). Parsed to
  each section's end in all 50 library puppet files.
- Skinning: bind world = parent world · local (GH 0x1402261c0); a vertex is Σ weight ·
  world(pose) · bindWorld⁻¹ · position, on the CPU, in the mesh's own y-up space (PR #625 negated
  the x and z angles; WE doesn't). Skinned z is flattened (inferred, as PR #625).
- Layers (GH 0x140228470): from the bind pose, each visible layer in order on its own clock
  (dt · rate; loop wraps, mirror bounces, single stops: GH 0x1401d4d00 / 0x1401d6a00). The
  animation is sampled between frames ⌊t·fps⌋ and the next (nlerp; GH 0x1401a00a0) and mixed in:
  normal = lerp (pose, sample, weight) (GH 0x140223b90), additive = pose + (sample − bind) ·
  weight with the rotation nlerp (1, sample · bind⁻¹, weight) · pose (GH 0x140224390; the scale
  and the product's order are inferred). The weight is blend × the blendin / blendout ramps over
  min (length / 2, blendtime) (GH 0x140291f60). `additive`, `blendin`, `blendout` and `blendtime`
  are parsed now and a layer is visible by default (WE's constructor GH 0x140291d20) (G06, G08).
- `attachment` (G09): a child pinned to its parent puppet's attachment is placed in the
  attachment's space — the bone's posed world · the MDAT matrix — under the parent's transform
  (looked up by name in GH 0x14020be30, applied in GH 0x1401b5170). It was ignored, so attached
  hair and heads sat off their characters.
- autosize grows the canvas to hold the mesh in every frame (PR #625's approach).
- A puppet without effects draws its only pass straight to the scene: its mesh is now mapped into
  the layer's scene rectangle there; it was drawn in layer pixels with the scene's projection.

Not ported: GPU skinning (SKINNING / g_Bones), bone alpha (SKINNING_ALPHA), blend shapes (MDLE,
MDMP), IK, physics bones, root motion, animation events, script layer control.

Origin: ours (the parsing and autosize follow upstream PR #625, Almamu/linux-wallpaperengine,
closed unmerged; checked against WE)
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B12 (G06–G09)
